        {
          "username": "Mostafa Elmankabady",
          "rating": 3,
          "contributor_id": "106293452338739123702",
          "description": "Halal Indian restaurant serving many choices of Indian do food, I will categorize my review into some parts as follows\n1- place\nThis is the most appealing point, as it is difficult to find a halal restaurant in this area, also it has an outside tables, and it is good if you prefer eating outdoors (I personally prefer to), It has a washing sink, the toilet is a bit difficult but if you ask them they will give you the keys for the toilet, it is next to the restaurant.\n2- Food\nThe food quantity was enough for a hungry person (I ordered the \"habibi set' for dinner), I am attaching some images for the set, I have a comment about seekh  kebab, it is very tinder and tasty but I think it doesn't contain much meat. I prefer mutton curry and butter chicken curry, I tried keema curry but it contains more dal than chicken or meat keema, the tandoori chicken is at its best, nan is big and I think 1 nan would suffice.\n3- Staff\nThis is a confusing point, the staff are a bit different from the comments and reviews here, they are a bit stiff and not as I am used to, they serve the tissues and plates in a rude way, they threw the tissue on the table, instead of putting it decently, in the end they helped us a bit in answering some questions about the area.",
